💭 test: unoptimized
💭 A class's receiver is allocated before its initializer's arguments are evaluated. If evaluating an argument
💭 reraises, the initializer, which is what would make it own the receiver, is never entered, so the receiver must
💭 still be released, without running a destructor over its uninitialized fields.
